{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "88", "x": 0.902607035282835, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.031136213320800684, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "But there were still obstacles. In the 1930s, few grocery stores could afford to buy", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.8262949696233941, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "freezers for a market that wasn't established yet. So, Birdseye leased inexpensive", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.8263307508322719, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "freezer cases to them. He also leased insulated railroad cars so that he could ship", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.8262077208877061, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "his products nationwide. However, few consumers had freezers large enough or", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.8260774116714202, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "efficient enough to take advantage of the products.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.5282458041918968, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Sales increased in the early 1940s, when World War II gave a boost to the frozen", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2746735439806541, "w": 0.8259902654606861, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "food industry because tin was being used for munitions. Canned foods were", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3030039694975767, "w": 0.8260773091464664, "h": 0.018822616509687834, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "rationed to save tin for the war effort, while frozen foods were abundant and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.33133430071101805, "w": 0.8258594436196312, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "cheap. Finally, by the 1950s, refrigerator technology had developed far enough to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3596646507851557, "w": 0.8262142824847497, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "make these appliances affordable for the average family. By 1953, 33 million US", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.38799500085929334, "w": 0.8260336335161456, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "families owned a refrigerator, and manufacturers were gradually increasing the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.41632538865482344, "w": 0.8261423099671786, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "size of the freezer compartments in them.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4446557764503536, "w": 0.42806436578114837, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "1950s families were also looking for convenience at mealtimes, so the moment", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.48280040298518045, "w": 0.8259684276455257, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "was right for the arrival of the 'TV Dinner'. Swanson Foods was a large, nationally", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5111307907807106, "w": 0.8260333259412842, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "recognized producer of canned and frozen poultry. In 1954, the company adapted", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5394611408548482, "w": 0.8267836035532278, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "some of Birdseye's freezing techniques, and with the help of a clever name and a", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5677915286503784, "w": 0.8259684276455257, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "huge advertising budget, it launched the first 'TV Dinner'. This consisted of frozen", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5961219164459085, "w": 0.8262516015679346, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "turkey, potatoes and vegetables served in the same segmented aluminum tray", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6244523042414386, "w": 0.8259249570651125, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "that was used by airlines. The product was an instant success. Within a year,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6527826543155762, "w": 0.8265758879968192, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Swanson had sold 13 million TV dinners. American consumers couldn't resist the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6811501222399445, "w": 0.8260379395642053, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "combination of a trusted brand name, a single-serving package and the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7094804723140822, "w": 0.8265333401409902, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "convenience of a meal that could be ready after only 25 minutes in a hot oven. By", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7378108223882198, "w": 0.8264578817749899, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "1959, Americans were spending $2.7 billion annually on frozen foods, and half a", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7661412479051425, "w": 0.8258377083294246, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "billion of that was spent on ready-prepared meals such as the TV Dinner.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7944715979792801, "w": 0.7403501975604597, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Today, the US frozen food industry has a turnover of over $67 billion annually, with", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8325914792806198, "w": 0.8266613938082925, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "$26.6 billion of that sold to consumers for home consumption. The remaining $40", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8609465745882446, "w": 0.8261859855974996, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "billion in frozen food sales come through restaurants, cafeterias, hospitals and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8892770001051672, "w": 0.8260335309911918, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "schools, and that represents a third of the total food service sales.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9176073501793048, "w": 0.6764518276764677, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}